        "name": "sn3ro",
        "email": "zak.darek@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T23:13:47Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(machines): Shapeoko 5 Pro and X-Carve hobby routers on the Grbl 1.1 post\n\nSix library machines from the makers' public pages:\n- Carbide 3D Shapeoko 5 Pro 4x4, 4x2, 2x2 (travel 1237/623 mm, Z 155 mm;\n  the router is the owner's choice, so no spindle is stated);\n- Inventables X-Carve 2021 1000 mm (749.3 x 749.3 x 114.3 mm, Makita\n  10,000-30,000 rpm, 0.8 kW);\n- Inventables X-Carve Pro 4x4 and 4x2 (1219.2 x 1219.2 / 609.6 x 101.6 mm,\n  VFD 8,000-24,000 rpm, 1.5 kW).\nNo maker states axis rates or where machine Z0 sits, so the files state\nneither: the Grbl post lifts in the work offset and stops with M0 for\neach tool change. The Onefinity frames wait for a confirmed controller\ndialect.\n\nRefs #3071\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
